{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneFpnBracket","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneFpnBracket","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":8,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneFpnBracket.passesFpnBracket_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneFpnBracket.passesFpnBracket_iff","kind":"theorem","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneFpnBracket.lean#L62-L65","doc":"**Membership is decidable margin both sides.** For a candidate `f_pn`, passing is equivalent to\nbeating both bounds — restating the gate as the conjunction a checker evaluates. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneFpnBracket.ame_strictly_bracketed","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneFpnBracket.ame_strictly_bracketed","kind":"theorem","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneFpnBracket.lean#L54-L60","doc":"**The experimental value is strictly bracketed.** The AME-exact `f_pn ≈ 0.58776` passes the gate\n— the `W_(2,1)`-derived bracket strictly contains the measured deuteron interface fraction, so an\nindex that lands the bracket is deuteron-consistent. This is the target-(3) content: the bracket is\n*about* the right number. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneFpnBracket.fpnBracket_width_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneFpnBracket.fpnBracket_width_pos","kind":"theorem","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneFpnBracket.lean#L50-L52","doc":"**The bracket has positive width** — the size of the falsifiable margin. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneFpnBracket.fpnBracket_nondegenerate","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneFpnBracket.fpnBracket_nondegenerate","kind":"theorem","line":45,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneFpnBracket.lean#L45-L48","doc":"**The bracket is non-degenerate** (`lower < upper`) — it has a genuine falsifiable margin, not a\npoint. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneFpnBracket.PassesFpnBracket","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneFpnBracket.PassesFpnBracket","kind":"def","line":41,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneFpnBracket.lean#L41-L43","doc":"**The deuteron `f_pn` bracket gate.** A candidate index passes iff its predicted deuteron\ninterface fraction lands strictly inside the `W_(2,1)`-derived bracket. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneFpnBracket.fpnAME","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneFpnBracket.fpnAME","kind":"def","line":38,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneFpnBracket.lean#L38-L39","doc":"The **AME-exact** deuteron interface fraction `f_pn ≈ 0.58776`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneFpnBracket.fpnUpper","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneFpnBracket.fpnUpper","kind":"def","line":34,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneFpnBracket.lean#L34-L36","doc":"**Upper bracket bound** for the deuteron `f_pn`, from the algebraic `W_(2,1)` at q₀ `≈ 0.66067`\n(#2503 / #2528 consumer). Cited (q₀-derived), not Lean-derived. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneFpnBracket.fpnLower","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneFpnBracket.fpnLower","kind":"def","line":30,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneFpnBracket.lean#L30-L32","doc":"**Lower bracket bound** for the deuteron `f_pn`, from the algebraic `W_(2,1)` at q₀: the LP-dual\n`a_K/R` ratio `≈ 0.39479017` (witness `a-K-via-lp-dual`). Cited (q₀-derived), not Lean-derived. ","signatureChunk":0}]}